{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_v23rc3s4t2lq6lc2annafpw7zekfpe7cfjlyb4vuydokzo3w4vdq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What was verified\n\n**Phase A — artifacts** (`translation/SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`)\n- 31 exported C symbols, all mechanically enumerated from `nm -D`; struct layouts cross-checked against gcc 11.5 (`c2Simplex` = 152 bytes, `a@0 b@36 c@72 d@108 div@144 count@148`, etc.).\n- **93 error-surface rows** — the library has *no* error channel (no `assert`, `return -1`, `errno`), so the rejection surface is null-pointer sentinels, `switch` fallbacks, out-of-range enums/counts, and unguarded division.\n- **72 configuration rows** — the 3×3 type grid × transforms × `use_radius` × cache mode × NULL-out masks × separation regimes, plus every arm of `c22`/`c23`/`c2D`/`c2L`/`c2Witness` driven directly.\n\n**Phases B–D — 113 differential tests**, both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`, everything compared bit-for-bit (`to_bits()`), across release + dev × default + `--no-default-features`. Symbol diff is empty in all four.\n\n## Real divergences found and fixed\n\n1. **Float operand ordering (the big one).** gcc at `-O0` does *not* consistently put the left C operand in the SSE destination register — in `c2Dot` it computes `a.x*b.x` with `a.x` as destination but `a.y*b.y` with `b.y`, then adds with the *second* product as destination. Since `addss`/`mulss` return the destination's NaN payload, LLVM's different (and freely commuted) choices diverged: `c2MulrvT({1,0}, {-inf, NaN})` gave `0x7fcc58dd` instead of `0xffc00000`. Fixed by replacing every `+ - * /` on `f32` with inline-asm primitives whose destination is pinned, each call site naming the register gcc actually chose (read off `objdump -d`).\n\n2. **`c2Support(NULL, 0, d)`** — C loads `verts[0]` before checking `count`, so it faults; LLVM deleted the dead load and Rust quietly returned `0`. Fixed with `read_volatile`; both now SIGSEGV.\n\n3. **Dev-profile crash signal** — libcore's `ub_checks` turned NULL dereferences into SIGABRT vs the C's SIGSEGV. Fixed via documented `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false`.\n\n4. **`FLT_EPSILON²`** was an approximate decimal literal; now spelled exactly, with a `const { assert! }` block checking all ten float constants against the C `.so`'s `.rodata`.\n\n## Documented as genuinely untestable (5 rows)\n\n`c2GJK` with an out-of-range `C2_TYPE`, `cache->count >= 5`, and out-of-range cache vertex indices make the C read **uninitialised stack** (for `count >= 5`, `verts[4]` literally overlaps the C's own `pB` proxy at `-0x150(%rbp)`). The C's answer isn't stable run-to-run and can fault, so those cases run in forked children asserting only what's meaningful — the deterministic Rust side never faults — with the measured C behaviour recorded in `ERRORS.md`.\n\nAlso noted honestly: the `while (iter < 20)` cap is dead code — 2.2 M randomized configs plus a hill-climb search never exceeded `iter == 6`.\n\n`./verify.sh` reruns everything end to end."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1030,"cache_read_input_tokens":351141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1030,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b1f148d-ef0b-41b5-bb8a-00c30dfd166e","uuid":"278e6e12-3a44-4597-a815-f8716dfcd843","timestamp":"2026-08-27T10:08:14.426Z"}
